# Weekly unattended Galacticus audit, Saturday morning, ending before the Saturday-evening
# usage reset (19:00 PST / 20:00 PDT; AUDIT_STOP_AT=18:00 in the config).
# Install with `scrontab -e` and paste these lines (adjust the partition, resources and path).
# The job's allocation is where builds and models run, so size it as for an interactive job:
# about -j24 per 128 GB (machines.md).
#SCRON --partition=dmtheory
#SCRON --job-name=galacticus-audit
#SCRON --cpus-per-task=32
#SCRON --mem=128G
#SCRON --time=13:00:00
#SCRON --output=/scratch/abenson/auditwork/runs/scron-%j.out
# (scrontab runs the command line as given. To start a run by hand as a batch job, use
#  sbatch <same options> --wrap "<full path to runAudit.sh>"; a plain `sbatch runAudit.sh`
#  runs a copy from Slurm's spool directory, which can not find the tools beside it.)
47 6 * * 6 $HOME/galacticusDevTools/codeAudits/auditLoop/runAudit.sh
